      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is adding a missing check that had been allowing RGBx formats to be created previously.  These could use an RGBA8 texture that would pass `isRenderable(texInfo)`, and separately `areColorTypeAndTextureInfoCompatible(kRGB_888x, RGBA8)` would pass because they can be sampled as `.rgb1`. There was never a consideration of compatible w/ renderable.\n\nGanesh has this check, but also had more options to support rendering to RGBx because GL and native Vulkan support RGB8 and RGBX8 formats. WebGPU and native metal do not, so chrome on graphite will not be able to render to RGBx.",
